      "ground_truth_answer": "The LCM(3) is a landing craft. I'd say LC rules apply, particularly this one quoted below. This rule does address the aforementioned uncertainty about the 25% MP expenditure. What I don't know is why an LTV4 is being cited here in reference to the question, instead of the data for LCM(3) and landing craft? I guess the unloading procedure could be similar for the lighter vehicles that the LTV4 can carry per chapter G, but it can't carry the Shermans. \n\nAs for the cost, I agree that more than 50% of the total cost of the vehicle to leave the LC is used, but less than 75%, so that would mean 3/4 of the points are spent. I don't think this is staggered incrementally but is totalled up. \n\n[ EDIT -- USA Vehicle note 51 speaks of MP allotment and movement allotment in the same paragraph. Note that while MF and MP are defined in the index as \"measures of movement capability\" (no mention of \"allotment\"), MF allotment is adequately described in A4.11 and MP allotment is not so adequately described in D1.1. There is NO general definition of movement allotment, though it is used in A4.1, D12.5, USA Vehicle Note 51, Korean Vehicle Note 25. We can deduce that movement allotment really means MF allotment or MP allotment, depending on the unit type. IMO \"movement allotment\" should be added to the Index and defined. ]\n\n12.4 (UN)LOADING: Except as stated otherwise, normal Vehicle\u2014not Boat\u2014(un)loading rules (D6.4-.5; D8.5) apply to LC and their Passengers. A LC Passenger may unload into an enemy-occupied hex. If a LC is Aground (or is Beached across a hexside that is not within its VCA), units may unload from it only into its hex, and do so by expending 25% (FRU) of their MF/MP allotment (plus COT MP if it is a vehicle). There is no D2.14 penalty cost for the presence of the LC in the Location, but Overstacking will apply when a vehicle [EXC: motorcycle] is in the same Location as a LC but is not a Passenger on one. A unit wishing to load onto an Aground LC must be in (or enter, expending that Location's COT to do so\u2014plus, if it is a vehicle, one extra MP for the presence of the LC; D2.14) that LC's Location, then expend 25% (FRU) of its MF/MP allotment (plus, if it is a vehicle, one MP as the LC's COT and one MP to Stop).",
