      "generated_answer": "The rule A20.21 prohibits any movement by a unit which is adjacent to an enemy unit at the start of its Rout Phase. However, rule A20.3 allows the prohibition of enemy units from being able to Rally or Rout away from an enemy unit if \"No Quarter\" has been declared.\n\nLow Crawl is a form of movement, and the prohibition stated in rule A20.21 takes precedence over the option of Low Crawl. Hence, even if \"No Quarter\" has been declared, units adjacent to an enemy unit cannot use Low Crawl during their Rout Phase as they are still prohibited from moving by A20.21. \n\n[Source: pdfcoffee.com_asl-2nd-edition-core-rules-pdf-free.pdf | Priority: P1 | Rule: A20.21, A20.3]",
      "ground_truth_answer": "Why are you equating Low Crawl with being ADJACENT????\n\n10.52 LOW CRAWL: Low Crawl is a rout of one Location which requires \nthe entire MF allotment of the routing unit (but is still considered a form of \nAssault Movement should the routing unit enter a FFE Blast Area). A rout-\ning unit using Low Crawl cannot be Interdicted. Low Crawl cannot be used \nto enter Marsh or a Water Obstacle, or in any stream unless dry. Low Crawl \ncannot be used to exit an enemy-occupied Location [EXC: Night (E1.54)]. \nAll other Rout provisions apply unchanged to Low Crawl, e.g., rout must still \nbe towards the nearest woods/building Location within 6 MF.\n\nNothing in 10.52 requires a unit that wants to Low Crawl be ADJACENT to an enemy unit (Known or otherwise).\n\nA Routing Unit has these options:\n* If not subject to possible surrender, it designates its Rout target (nearest woods/building within 6 MF) and:\n1) Routs using its 6 MF (3 for Wounded Leader, etc). towards that target; if moving into Open Ground it may be subject to Interdiction (A10.53; A10.531).\n2) Declares Low Crawl and only Routs a single hex, AGAIN TOWARDS THE ROUT TARGET.\n\n*If No Quarter has NOT been declared and it begins the Rout phase adjacent to a KEU and cannot Rout in any way to avoid Interdiction, it Surrenders to that adjacent KEU.\n\n*If No Quarter HAS been declared and it begins the Rout phase adjacent to a KEU and cannot Rout in any way to avoid Interdiction, it does NOT Surrender and may either Rout using its 6 MF (taking the Interdiction MC(s)) or Low Crawl one hex and avoiding all Interdiction rolls.\n\nNote that if the broken unit begins the Rout phase adjacent to a KEU, but has a VALID Rout path that does _not_ subject it to Interdiction, it does ** NOT ** Surrender and can Rout via the first bullet above (either using full 6 MF or Low Crawling one hex ... but both still must be towards it's designated Rout target).",
